  "articleBody": "It's a common frustration: you've got new door casing, but it just doesn't seem to sit right around your existing door jamb or against the wall. Don't worry, you're not alone! This often happens because door openings or walls aren't perfectly plumb or square, especially in older homes. The first thing we always do is carefully measure the actual opening, not just rely on standard dimensions. This helps us understand any existing irregularities. Then, it's about making precise cuts for the side and head pieces, ensuring they account for any slight variations in the opening. Sometimes, you might need to slightly adjust the casing to align perfectly with the jamb and the wall before fastening. If there are minor gaps, a bit of caulk can work wonders to create a seamless transition, and filling nail holes ensures a clean, finished appearance. The key is patience and precision. If you find yourself struggling with uneven jambs or walls, or if you want that truly seamless, professional look around all your doors, it's definitely a good idea to bring in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC. We've got the experience to make sure your door casing looks perfect, even in tricky situations, serving the greater Denver area.",
